  "scope": "Unchanged ZoneBorders, Zone, ZoneType, ZoneRestriction, RegionZone, ZoneBuilder, MapZone, ZoneMonitor, BankZone, KaramjaZone, ModeratorZone, MultiwayCombatZone, MusicZone, Region.java, MapDistance and Pulse on JDK 11; PulseRunner with one added import alias for its clock. Original text inserted at generation time: RegionManager.forId over its cache map and lock, RegionChunk.clear, Entity.isTeleBlocked, Pathfinder.isStandingIn, RandomFunction.RANDOM and normalRandDist(max, intensity), the Log enum, and Location's packed hash, region id forms, transform, toString, equals and hashCode. Everything else is a recording adapter: Entity, Player, NPC, Familiar and all their sub-objects, Item, Option, CombatStyle, RequestType, Rights, TeleportManager, the packet classes, the local entity queries and isTeleportPermitted of RegionManager, the rest of RegionChunk, Cache (no map archive is ever found, so Region.load stops after its lookup), DynamicRegion, the map parsers, Scenery, GameWorld, Repository, the log function, ServerConstants, and placeholder WildernessZone and DarkZone classes that exist only so ZoneBuilder compiles. MapZone.checkMulti reads the real wall clock: cases use combat times that are far from it. getRandomLoc draws from unseeded generators: only facts that do not depend on the draw are recorded. Not exercised: ZoneBuilder.startup, MapZone.cleanItems, Region.load beyond the archive lookup, the assemble lists, dynamic regions, self-referencing exception lists and region id lists beyond a few regions.",
